%S A398953 1229,2429,3029,3329,4529,6029,9779,11579,12779,13079,13379,16229,
%T A398953 16829,17429,18629,20729,23579,23879,25079,25379,26879,28079,30929,
%U A398953 31829,32429,33029,33329,34529,34829,37979,38879,39179,40979,41579,42779,45629,45929,46829,47129
%N A398953 Starts of runs of 32 successive 5-rough numbers that are squarefree.
%C A398953 32 is the largest possible length of such runs: at least one number in each run of 33 successive 5-rough numbers is divisible by 25 = 5^2, and thus it is not squarefree.
%C A398953 The asymptotic density of this sequence is (1/150) * Product_{p prime >= 7} (1 - 32/p^2) = 0.0008000600400436108945618... .
%H A398953 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A398953/b398953.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A398953 a(n) == 29 (mod 150) for all n.
%e A398953 1229 = A007310(410) is a term since A007310(410+i) is squarefree for each i in the range [0, 31].
%t A398953 q[k_] := Mod[k, 150] == 29 && AllTrue[Table[k + (6*i - 7 - (-1)^i)/2, {i, 1, 32}], SquareFreeQ]; Select[Range[48000], q]
%o A398953 (PARI) isok(k) = if(k % 150 != 29, 0, for(i = 1, 32, if(!issquarefree(k + (6*i - 7 - (-1)^i)/2), return(0))); 1);
%Y A398953 Subsequence of A005117, A007310 (5-rough numbers), A276378 (5-rough squarefree numbers), and A398952.
%Y A398953 Similar sequences: A007675, A398951, A398956.
%K A398953 nonn,easy,new
%O A398953 1,1
%A A398953 _Amiram Eldar_, Aug 15 2026
